sbe1v1k: dts: describe the WAN PHY LEDs

The RTL8261BE drives the WAN port's amber (LED0) and green (LED1) LEDs.
Describe them so the PHY driver registers them and netdev trigger rules
can be offloaded to the PHY (needs the RTL826x LED support in
generic/hack-6.18/744). Default rules are set in board.d/01_leds.

From hurrian/openwrt-w1700k 4824815669 "sbe1v1k: add phy leds config"
(Kenneth Kasilag).

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
@@ -502,6 +502,24 @@
 		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 41 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		reset-assert-us = <40000>;
 		reset-deassert-us = <150000>;
+
+		/* WAN port LEDs, driven by the PHY (netdev trigger offload) */
+		leds {
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+
+			led@0 {
+				reg = <0>;
+				color = <LED_COLOR_ID_AMBER>;
+				function = LED_FUNCTION_WAN;
+			};
+
+			led@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+				color = <LED_COLOR_ID_GREEN>;
+				function = LED_FUNCTION_WAN;
+			};
+		};
 	};
 
 	ethernet-phy-package@16 {
